    <p>A characterful red-brick Victorian hall on the triangular village green. Built in 1885, it was known as Chafecote until its owner, Tom Burns, gave it to the village in 1947, and only later took the name Rous Lench Village Hall.</p>
    <p>Today it's a registered charity run by volunteer trustees. It hosts public events through the year and is available for private hire.</p>
    <p>To enquire about hiring, email <a href="mailto:info@rouslench.com">info@rouslench.com</a> or call 01386 896155.</p>
    <p><a href="https://rouslench.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit the Rous Lench website &rarr;</a></p>
